Installation Instructions

rewindOS – Experimental Installation Guide

Current status

rewindOS is currently an early development prototype. A complete bootable ISO and Windows-style installer are not available yet.

Requirements

- 64-bit x86 PC
- USB drive (for future installation)
- Virtual machine software such as QEMU or VirtualBox (recommended for testing)

Current development build

1. Download the rewindOS source ZIP from the GitHub Releases page.
2. Extract the ZIP.
3. Read the "README.md" file.
4. Follow the build instructions in "docs/BUILDING.md".
5. Compile the kernel using the provided build system.
6. Boot only through a supported development environment once the required boot files are available.

Important warnings

- The current kernel ELF is not a bootable ISO.
- Do not attempt to install it directly onto your PC.
- Do not format or modify your Windows drive.
- Test experimental builds in a virtual machine with a disposable virtual disk.

Future installation

A Windows-style USB installer is planned. It will eventually provide language selection, disk selection, installation progress and first-time account setup.

Thank you for trying rewindOS!
